@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Game Search — Selection Map (what kind of game is it?)
' Synthesis: which search applies, and when the usual tree assumption breaks
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert\ngame structure?" as H

component "Minimax + alpha-beta\nalternating, perfect information" as MM <<app>>
component "MCTS / UCT\nsampled rollouts, huge branching" as MCTS <<host>>
component "Matrix game per node\nsimultaneous moves" as SIM <<error>>
component "Belief sampling\nhidden state" as BEL <<async>>

H ARROW_MAIN MM : turns alternate,\nboard fully visible
H ARROW_MAIN MCTS : branching too wide\nto enumerate
H ARROW_ERROR SIM : both sides commit at once
H ARROW_QUEUE BEL : some state is hidden

note bottom of SIM
  **The tree assumption is load-bearing.** Minimax
  and vanilla MCTS both assume "my move, then
  yours". If both sides commit simultaneously,
  there is no such tree — each decision point is a
  matrix game needing an equilibrium or a
  regret-minimizing policy, not a max.
  ----
  If state is also hidden, the object you evaluate
  is a **belief, not a position** — that is the
  Stratego/poker family, handled in
  ""../imperfect-information-games/"".
  ----
  ""mcts-uct.puml"" covers the sampling engine;
  reactive alternatives that skip search entirely
  live at ""_spec/study-cases/_substrate/reactive-control/"".
end note
@enduml
